    "turn_text": "I have heard that time and again through different relief efforts after hurricanes over the years. What a difference, a hot cup of coffee. a hot meal makes. Just it just just does. So again, that's at seven o'clock this morning out in Perry. There are a couple of other efforts going on. I think Grant, you mentioned that the Leon County Sheriff's Office is organizing something. I think you said somebody was organizing something you said it in the news yesterday. that there was a relief effort being organized. I thought it might have been Leon County, but it could have been Taylor County or some other county, but there was a relief effort going on that you can take part in. We'll pass along what we know and kind of go from there. But at any rate, Moving on to other things. Yesterday, Keith Olberman stepped in it again. And I want to highlight this because I responded. I, I had to. Olberman decides after Riley gains is, uh, you know, she's obviously making a defense for women's sports. and making a defense for the women's bill of rights, which suggests that males and females possess biological differences that are immutable. Oberman posts on his Twitter page, can you just address the reality and move past it? You sucked at swimming. That's why you lost. First of all, she was an all-American. Secondly, she got, she tied with Leah Thomas in an NCAA, I think national championship. She was the SEC female scholar athlete of the year in 2022. She's pretty good. She was invited to Olympic trials. And I just replied with those points. And I said it's a far better resume than constantly being introduced as former. Former this, former that, former, that's Keith's title, former. Others replied as well, I'm sorry, your statement should be directed toward a dude named Leah Thomas. He sucks at swimming against biological males so much that he decided to identify his females so he could win. How sexist and sad, both you and Leah. The vitriol and venom of people like